content:
The bug is that both `always @(*)` blocks only assign their outputs in one branch, which infers **latches** (and leaves the outputs undefined/`x` when the condition is false). The fix is to give every output a definite value in all cases (i.e., add the `else` branches / default assignments), turning the logic into pure combinational gates.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input      cpu_overheated,
    output reg shut_off_computer,
    input      arrived,
    input      gas_tank_empty,
    output reg keep_driving
);

    // Fix: assign the output in every case so no latch is inferred.
    always @(*) begin
        if (cpu_overheated)
            shut_off_computer = 1'b1;
        else
            shut_off_computer = 1'b0;
    end

    // Fix: assign the output in every case so no latch is inferred.
    always @(*) begin
        if (~arrived)
            keep_driving = ~gas_tank_empty;
        else
            keep_driving = 1'b0;
    end

endmodule
```
